ArchiveEntry "3-Machine pH D2<0: LARGE-SIGNAL sublevel INVARIANCE, PARAMETRIC in d"

/*
 * 3-machine analog of theorem_ph_bridge_invariant_parametric (the 2-machine
 * "missing quadrant"). Line 1-2-3, D1=D3=K=1, MIDDLE machine non-passive D2=-d.
 * The sublevel set {V < 1/25} is positively invariant on the large-signal box
 * c1,c2 in [4/5,1], for ALL d in (0, 3/20], with d SYMBOLIC.  V is the pH
 * Lyapunov function of theorem_3machine_linear (constant h=1/5).
 *
 * KeYmaera X STATUS: NOT machine-verified -- the slab dI TIMES OUT (>350s).
 *
 * The naive dI keeps the circle equalities s1^2+c1^2=1, s2^2+c2^2=1 in the
 * evolution domain -> 9-variable QE over a variety, times out (theorem_3machine).
 * Slab trick (as in the 2-machine case): V' is MULTILINEAR in (c1,c2), and V'<=0
 * holds on the whole box c1,c2 in [4/5,1] (theorem_3machine_descent_parametric:
 * all 4 vertices NSD for d in (0,3/20], PROVED). The dynamics conserve s1^2+c1^2
 * and s2^2+c2^2, so every physical trajectory with c1,c2>=4/5 lies in the box.
 * Taking the evolution domain to be the box {4/5<=c1<=1, 4/5<=c2<=1} (no
 * equalities) reduces the dI obligation to the box descent QE.
 *
 * BUT for 3 machines this box QE is in 7 variables (d,w1,w2,w3,s1,s2,c1,c2) with
 * TWO cosines (bilinear box), and Z3 times out (>350s). The 2-machine analog
 * closed in 0.58s (5 vars, one cosine); the third machine's second cosine
 * doubles the box dimension and breaks the dI's monolithic QE. The MATH holds
 * (descent on the 4 vertices + multilinearity => V'<=0 on the box => invariance);
 * only the automated KeYmaera X closure is beyond the Z3 backend here. The
 * achievable parametric large-signal result is the DESCENT (the companion file).
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real da; Real db; Real dc;
  Real w1; Real w2; Real w3;
  Real s1; Real c1; Real s2; Real c2;
End.

Problem
  \forall d (
    0 < d & d <= 3/20 &
    s1^2 + c1^2 = 1 & s2^2 + c2^2 = 1 & c1 >= 4/5 & c2 >= 4/5 &
    w1^2+w2^2+w3^2+2*(1-c1)+2*(1-c2)+(1/5)*(s1^2+s2^2)+(1+d)*(w1*s1-w3*s2)+((1+3*d)/4)*w2*(s1-s2) < 1/25
    ->
    [{da' = w1, db' = w2, dc' = w3,
      w1' = -w1 - s1,
      w2' = d*w2 + s1 - s2,
      w3' = -w3 + s2,
      s1' = c1*(w1 - w2), c1' = -s1*(w1 - w2),
      s2' = c2*(w2 - w3), c2' = -s2*(w2 - w3)
      & c1 >= 4/5 & c1 <= 1 & c2 >= 4/5 & c2 <= 1}]
    w1^2+w2^2+w3^2+2*(1-c1)+2*(1-c2)+(1/5)*(s1^2+s2^2)+(1+d)*(w1*s1-w3*s2)+((1+3*d)/4)*w2*(s1-s2) < 1/25
  )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  allR(1);
  implyR(1);
  dI(1)
End.

End.
